  Question 7 — falsifier. Byte-identical digest achievable? Sources of difference:
  (a) FP summation order: zeros contribute exactly 0 → sums identical IF loop order over real points preserved (ascending frame) ✓ and if skipped rather than added — either way bit-identical (adding +0.0 to a finite double is exact; signed-zero edge: sum is always ≥ 0 so no -0 issues). mean/invnorm identical IF G identical. dot identical (skipped entries add nothing). So FP order is NOT the problem — the design can preserve evaluation order.
  (b) The digest breakers are REPRESENTATION-level value changes, not order:
